Z||000167||fierobear||07-21-2001||03:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Stage-2GT:<BR><B> Fiero Bear, how baout making it an action drama with Archie being played by Martin Shean and George played by Marlon Brando? The title could be "APOLOGY NOW". I really like this. We could go on forever trying new charactors and titles. Keep em' coming folks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>S2GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Apology Now - LOL! Good one. We could have some fun with this!<P>"I love the smell of Kevlar in the morning...smells like...motorsports"<P>If we're going to make an action flick, we need Jesse Ventura as Archie and Charles Bronson as George.||||reg||1
Z||000168||Stage-2GT||07-21-2001||03:09 PM||||  By the time you get done reading this, it will be to late........BOOMMMMMMMMM!!!!!<P>WhaaaahaaaaaWhaahahhaahhaahhaa!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000169||Mach10||07-21-2001||03:33 PM||||"I'm gonna give ya ta tha count a ten to refund me the clutch before I pump your guts fulla lead... One... Two... TEN!" buddabuddabuddabudda*HAHAHAHAHAHA*buddabuddabudda-tinkletinkletinkle...<BR>"Keep the clutch you filthy animal"<P>I say that we also feature a Toaster from space.<P>Time to unleash My Opinion!<BR>First of all, my experience in this thread is that Archie is VERY defensive, and quick to lash out at any percieved slight. I don't know him, and I haven't had any problems with him or his product. However, his business is well established, and of the 200-300 Archie-Jobs I've seen, I've heard 3, maybe 4 complaints. 96%-97% success rate is better than most surgeries. I haven't dealt with Archie himself yet, so I can't comment on his professionalism.<BR>Now, that having been said, the posts that Archie has made in this particular thread have been rude and unproffessional. Given that this has been a long-running issue, some may be forgiven, as things tend to build up. That's just my view. Archie hasn't lost MY business YET.<BR>2) George has been nothing but professional about this whole deal, on this forum. However, his customer service skills could be a little better. The willingness to wash his hands of a deal that he initiated doesn't speak well. That said, he doesn't have any legal responsibility to Archie, based on what I've seen here. HOWEVER, in terms of customer satisfaction, and service, he should have been more involved. It's all fair and good to take back an item if it self-destructs, and THEN determine that it was due to mis-use. HOWEVER, to my understanding, the clutch never left Archies shop. That was a mistake. If the clutch died because of misuse, then Archie is owed NOTHING. But the attempt MUST HAVE BEEN MADE. Since George initiated the deal, he should have stayed in it, unless it was made perfectly clear that his business had nothing to do with it. As it was, it wasn't his product, but it was offered THROUGH GEORGE. This is important. This sets the expectation that George is responsible for all the RMAs. <BR>Again, I don't have all the facts.<BR>George: You have conducted yourself in a coureous and professional manner. I applaud you for that. In terms of service, I think that you should not have distanced yourself so much from the product, but that was your choice. You haven't lost business from me either.||||reg||7
